1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,300
(Previously on...)
You didn't tell anyone I like BL, did you?

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,967
No, but on one condition.

3
00:00:05,067 --> 00:00:07,076
You have to eat lunch with
me every day from now on.

4
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:09,333
I'm counting on you for
the novel, Teacher Suzuki.

5
00:00:09,433 --> 00:00:10,233
Teacher?

6
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:11,000
Wait a sec, Serizawa.

7
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:13,276
What we just talked about is a
secret between Suzuki and me.

8
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:14,700
So annoying.

9
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:15,909
This makes absolutely no sense.

10
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:17,700
You'll get used to Serizawa in no time.

11
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,367
Oh, sorry.

12
00:00:19,633 --> 00:00:21,433
I just wanted to hear your voice.

13
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:22,767
Huh?

14
00:00:22,867 --> 00:00:26,167
I really don't deserve
to be called a teacher.

15
00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:28,267
The great parts of your novel, Suzuki...

16
00:00:28,367 --> 00:00:29,676
And the parts that make
my heart skip a beat...

17
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:31,233
Until you can see them for yourself...

18
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:33,333
I'll point them all out to you.

19
00:00:33,833 --> 00:00:35,267
Serizawa...

20
00:00:38,267 --> 00:00:40,033
Suzuki.

21
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:42,967
Morning.

22
00:00:43,367 --> 00:00:44,533
Morning.

23
00:00:44,633 --> 00:00:46,200
Brought your lunch today?

24
00:00:46,767 --> 00:00:48,000
Yeah.

25
00:00:48,667 --> 00:00:50,767
Your lunch box is so cute, Suzuki.

26
00:00:50,867 --> 00:00:54,600
It's been two weeks since I started eating
lunch with The Popular Clique's Big Four.

27
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:56,133
Uh, sorry about this.

28
00:00:56,567 --> 00:00:58,467
I'm always crashing your lunch.

29
00:00:59,206 --> 00:01:01,273
No, it's totally fine.

30
00:01:01,367 --> 00:01:03,267
What's up man?

31
00:01:04,033 --> 00:01:05,600
Morning, Suzuki.

32
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:08,233
Morning, Serizawa.

33
00:01:10,533 --> 00:01:13,200
Teacher, how's the novel coming along?

34
00:01:14,467 --> 00:01:16,167
I've made a little progress.

35
00:01:16,267 --> 00:01:17,267
That's awesome!

36
00:01:17,367 --> 00:01:18,700
Let me read it later.

37
00:01:20,267 --> 00:01:23,000
Um, I'm right here, you know.

38
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:24,600
Oh, my bad, my bad.

39
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:27,467
By the way, what were you just
talking about with my Suzuki?

40
00:01:27,567 --> 00:01:29,967
He's not your Suzuki.

41
00:01:30,367 --> 00:01:31,667
Morning!

42
00:01:31,767 --> 00:01:32,367
Alright.

43
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:34,567
- Morning.
- That's way too much.

44
00:01:34,667 --> 00:01:37,067
Morning...

45
00:01:37,467 --> 00:01:41,800
Lately, my classmates have started
talking to me on their own.

46
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:42,733
What?

47
00:01:42,833 --> 00:01:43,567
A snack party?

48
00:01:43,667 --> 00:01:44,433
Yeah.

49
00:01:44,533 --> 00:01:46,467
I heard Koharu got them from a senior.

50
00:01:46,567 --> 00:01:47,667
Yeah, that's right.

51
00:01:47,767 --> 00:01:49,600
- She said everyone can share.
- Really?

52
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,267
- Thanks.
- Don't mention it.

53
00:01:51,367 --> 00:01:53,300
- So many kinds.
- Pick one.

54
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:54,520
Which one should I choose...

55
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,233
Suzuki, you'll have some too, right?

56
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:58,333
But...

57
00:01:59,233 --> 00:02:00,633
Come on, join us.

58
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:03,067
Come on, get over here.

59
00:02:04,167 --> 00:02:05,700
Okay, thanks.

60
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,067
Alright!

61
00:02:07,167 --> 00:02:09,733
Even though there are still
many things I'm not used to,

62
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:11,143
honestly, I'm having a pretty good time.

63
00:02:11,167 --> 00:02:11,933
I'll go with this one.

64
00:02:12,033 --> 00:02:12,767
Okay.

65
00:02:12,867 --> 00:02:13,700
Nice choice.

66
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:14,967
Looks delicious.

67
00:02:18,367 --> 00:02:19,200
Here.

68
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:20,033
Say ah!

69
00:02:20,133 --> 00:02:21,600
I can feed myself.

70
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:22,967
What's the big deal?

71
00:02:23,067 --> 00:02:24,867
I want to feed you too. Here, Suzuki.

72
00:02:24,967 --> 00:02:25,433
Say ah!

73
00:02:25,533 --> 00:02:26,433
- This is fun.
- Me too...

74
00:02:26,533 --> 00:02:27,633
Here, say ah...

75
00:02:27,733 --> 00:02:29,267
- Come on.
- Here...

76
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:30,300
I can feed myself!

77
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:31,467
- Ah...
- Come on.

78
00:02:31,567 --> 00:02:32,333
- Me too...
- Got some right here.

79
00:02:32,433 --> 00:02:33,300
You guys.

80
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,633
Come on...

81
00:02:34,733 --> 00:02:37,367
Are you treating Suzuki
like a deer in Nara?

82
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,000
What, is an alien speaking?

83
00:02:41,833 --> 00:02:42,833
Hey!

84
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,500
I'm the one speaking.

85
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:45,533
Seems like it.

86
00:02:45,633 --> 00:02:46,700
Oh, thanks.

87
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:47,833
What are you guys doing?

88
00:02:47,933 --> 00:02:49,233
We're going to be late.

89
00:02:49,867 --> 00:02:50,867
Huh?

90
00:02:50,933 --> 00:02:51,600
I'll take this then.

91
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,367
Yeah, here.

92
00:02:53,667 --> 00:02:54,567
Here.

93
00:02:54,667 --> 00:02:55,300
This is the biggest piece.

94
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,400
Ah...

95
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,733
Hey, um... is that...?

96
00:03:07,333 --> 00:03:08,700
Yuma, this is really good.

97
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:11,200
- Really?
- Yeah, here, say ah!

98
00:03:12,667 --> 00:03:15,000
By the way, "Suzubi"...

99
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:16,200
Suzubi?

100
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:18,933
When did you get so close
to Serizawa and the guys?

101
00:03:19,033 --> 00:03:21,133
- Huh?
- I've actually been a bit curious.

102
00:03:21,233 --> 00:03:22,709
You guys just suddenly got super tight.

103
00:03:22,733 --> 00:03:24,000
Yeah.

104
00:03:38,867 --> 00:03:42,367
Can I really consider them my friends?

105
00:03:51,467 --> 00:03:52,500
Pass it to me!

106
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:53,700
Here.

107
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,633
- Huh?
- Takeuchi.

108
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:57,300
It wasn't me, it wasn't me!

109
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,533
- It wasn't me, it wasn't me!
- You totally did that.

110
00:04:00,633 --> 00:04:03,067
How dare you mess with me!

111
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:08,500
To call us friends, we live in
completely different worlds.

112
00:04:50,967 --> 00:04:54,000
"Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me"

113
00:04:55,967 --> 00:04:58,700
(Episode 3)

114
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:02,067
At the end of the day,
what even defines a friend?

115
00:05:04,867 --> 00:05:07,933
(Friend Standard)

116
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:14,980
"What defines a friend? What do you guys think?
1. Accepts the real you 2. Fun to be around."

117
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:18,300
The real me...

118
00:05:20,667 --> 00:05:24,367
By the way, what's the deal with Suzuki?

119
00:05:24,467 --> 00:05:25,067
Right?

120
00:05:25,167 --> 00:05:27,043
How did he suddenly get so tight
with The Popular Clique's Big Four?

121
00:05:27,067 --> 00:05:30,367
It makes absolutely no sense. They're
in a totally different league than Suzuki.

122
00:05:43,533 --> 00:05:44,800
Suzuki!

123
00:05:45,533 --> 00:05:47,133
Finally found you.

124
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Serizawa.

125
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:50,667
So this is where you've been.

126
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:52,533
I've been looking all over for you.

127
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:55,200
Wh-What's wrong?

128
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:56,200
Nothing.

129
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:58,233
You just left without saying a word.

130
00:05:58,333 --> 00:05:59,600
I felt so lonely.

131
00:06:00,967 --> 00:06:01,867
Sorry.

132
00:06:01,967 --> 00:06:03,933
You guys were having
such a great time chatting,

133
00:06:04,033 --> 00:06:05,633
I felt a bit awkward interrupting.

134
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:09,867
Next time, at least say a
proper goodbye to me.

135
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:11,900
Yeah.

136
00:06:11,967 --> 00:06:13,800
By the way, are you free today?

137
00:06:14,367 --> 00:06:15,367
Uh...

138
00:06:16,533 --> 00:06:17,200
Yeah.

139
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:19,409
Then do you want to go sing karaoke
with everyone right now?

140
00:06:19,433 --> 00:06:20,133
With everyone?

141
00:06:20,233 --> 00:06:22,333
- Yeah.
- Karaoke?

142
00:06:22,433 --> 00:06:23,800
Here, this way.

143
00:06:31,133 --> 00:06:32,000
Hey.

144
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,400
Let's go, let's go.

145
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:34,767
Suzuki.

146
00:06:36,267 --> 00:06:37,267
Hey.

147
00:06:41,833 --> 00:06:43,967
Matsuno, what's wrong?

148
00:06:45,433 --> 00:06:47,233
Oh, nothing...

149
00:06:47,333 --> 00:06:49,333
Never mind, sorry.

150
00:06:50,467 --> 00:06:52,600
Wh-What should I do?

151
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:55,833
I had a moment of weakness
and just tagged along.

152
00:06:55,933 --> 00:07:01,067
But in front of The Popular Clique's Big
Four, I don't even know a single hype song.

153
00:07:01,167 --> 00:07:02,167
Cheers!

154
00:07:02,267 --> 00:07:04,167
I want to sing Chicken.

155
00:07:04,267 --> 00:07:05,700
What's that?

156
00:07:06,533 --> 00:07:08,600
Bump of Chicken, obviously!

157
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:09,367
"Bump of Chicken"?

158
00:07:09,467 --> 00:07:11,900
- And "Higedan".
- Your abbreviations are way too weird.

159
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,767
- Higedan?
- Official Hige Dandism!

160
00:07:13,867 --> 00:07:14,600
- What?
- Hige?

161
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:17,167
- Are you out of your mind?
- Hey...

162
00:07:17,267 --> 00:07:18,167
Here you go, Suzuki.

163
00:07:18,267 --> 00:07:20,100
Oh, thanks.

164
00:07:22,333 --> 00:07:24,333
What do you usually sing, Suzuki?

165
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:28,567
Uh, well...

166
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:30,767
What's wrong?

167
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:35,333
Actually, well...

168
00:07:36,367 --> 00:07:39,167
I'm not really used to karaoke.

169
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:44,567
And I don't think I've ever
sung in front of people before.

170
00:07:44,667 --> 00:07:46,567
Seriously? My bad.

171
00:07:46,667 --> 00:07:50,067
I'm not really familiar
with recent songs either.

172
00:07:54,767 --> 00:07:57,067
Then I'll help you look for one.

173
00:07:58,400 --> 00:07:59,400
Huh?

174
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:02,400
Here, hand it over.

175
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:06,633
First, press here.

176
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:08,800
Okay.

177
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:10,167
Then press here.

178
00:08:10,267 --> 00:08:11,267
Okay.

179
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,300
And then do this.

180
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:17,400
Oh, I can do it myself.

181
00:08:18,367 --> 00:08:19,433
It's fine.

182
00:08:19,533 --> 00:08:22,567
Come on, let's start from the "A" section.

183
00:08:23,367 --> 00:08:25,500
Tell me if you recognize any songs.

184
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:27,867
Time to dig in!

185
00:08:27,967 --> 00:08:29,233
Hey...

186
00:08:29,333 --> 00:08:30,033
You're eating way too much.

187
00:08:30,133 --> 00:08:30,633
What's the big deal?

188
00:08:30,733 --> 00:08:32,767
(Song Title: Hometown)
There's plenty left anyway.

189
00:08:32,867 --> 00:08:33,967
Huh?

190
00:08:34,433 --> 00:08:35,467
Oh.

191
00:08:35,567 --> 00:08:37,333
It's finally Suzuki's turn.

192
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:39,400
That's a really weird song choice.

193
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:40,933
I'm so nervous.

194
00:08:41,033 --> 00:08:42,143
- You got this, Suzuki!
- Awesome, awesome!

195
00:08:42,167 --> 00:08:43,433
Stand up and sing...

196
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:51,700
(Fishing for minnows in that river)

197
00:08:53,967 --> 00:08:55,467
Sorry, I really can't do this.

198
00:08:56,233 --> 00:08:57,633
Suzuki, are you okay?

199
00:08:57,733 --> 00:08:58,876
You don't have to force
yourself if you don't want to sing.

200
00:08:58,900 --> 00:08:59,333
Yeah.

201
00:08:59,433 --> 00:09:01,900
Here, want some fries?

202
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:04,500
Here, have some more fries.

203
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:05,733
Um.

204
00:09:05,833 --> 00:09:07,433
I'm going to grab a drink.

205
00:09:08,233 --> 00:09:09,933
Do you guys want anything?

206
00:09:10,667 --> 00:09:12,933
I'll take a melon soda.

207
00:09:13,033 --> 00:09:13,667
Melon soda it is.

208
00:09:13,767 --> 00:09:15,900
- Melon soda?
- Yep, melon soda.

209
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,080
Can I get an iced tea then?

210
00:09:17,167 --> 00:09:18,000
Sure.

211
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:19,740
- Could you grab me one too?
- You got it.

212
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,333
Here, it's all yours.

213
00:09:24,733 --> 00:09:25,367
Huh?

214
00:09:25,467 --> 00:09:26,533
What are you doing?

215
00:09:26,633 --> 00:09:27,433
Then I'll go with you.

216
00:09:27,533 --> 00:09:29,200
Hold on a sec.

217
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:30,533
You're up next.

218
00:09:30,633 --> 00:09:33,067
- Come on, sit down.
- Pick a song.

219
00:09:33,167 --> 00:09:34,676
- I'm gonna go get some drinks.
- Sorry about that.

220
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,109
- In that case...
- Aren't you gonna sing?

221
00:09:36,133 --> 00:09:37,167
- Hype it up!
- Okay.

222
00:09:37,433 --> 00:09:38,900
- Get the crowd going!
- Okay.

223
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,333
I'll sing backup then.

224
00:09:40,433 --> 00:09:40,967
You good?

225
00:09:41,067 --> 00:09:42,700
- Can you do it?
- Let me think.

226
00:09:43,733 --> 00:09:47,433
(Melon Soda)

227
00:09:48,233 --> 00:09:50,300
You guys actually invited me out.

228
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:53,967
I guess this is still too hard for me.

229
00:09:54,067 --> 00:09:55,176
You can sing for everyone next time.

230
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,400
- Why? You have to sing!
- No.

231
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:59,067
Nakamura's been hogging the mic anyway.

232
00:10:00,967 --> 00:10:02,633
Huh? Suzuki?

233
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:07,833
Wow, it really is Suzuki.

234
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:09,667
Long time no see.

235
00:10:11,233 --> 00:10:13,000
Um...

236
00:10:13,867 --> 00:10:15,200
Long time no see...

237
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:20,733
You're... not alone.

238
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:23,700
Yeah...

239
00:10:24,433 --> 00:10:26,833
I'm here with some classmates.

240
00:10:26,933 --> 00:10:27,833
Huh?

241
00:10:27,933 --> 00:10:30,800
Are you with Serizawa and his crew?

242
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:33,033
Yeah, pretty much.

243
00:10:33,133 --> 00:10:35,467
No way.

244
00:10:35,567 --> 00:10:38,067
I noticed something.

245
00:10:38,167 --> 00:10:42,000
Why have you been hanging out with
The Popular Clique's Big Four lately?

246
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:44,567
Oh, no, it just kind of happened.

247
00:10:44,667 --> 00:10:47,100
I can't believe you're
hanging with the A-listers.

248
00:10:49,133 --> 00:10:53,200
You're completely different
from them, aren't you?

249
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:54,567
That's insane.

250
00:10:54,667 --> 00:10:58,200
But aren't Serizawa and his crew
just messing with you?

251
00:10:58,300 --> 00:10:59,633
That sucks.

252
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:02,400
Hey, are you okay?

253
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:03,943
Are they treating you like an errand boy?

254
00:11:03,967 --> 00:11:05,800
Ah, probably.

255
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:07,467
That's definitely it.

256
00:11:07,567 --> 00:11:08,967
No, they're not like that...

257
00:11:09,067 --> 00:11:10,267
By the way, Suzuki.

258
00:11:11,133 --> 00:11:13,067
Are you still reading BL?

259
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:19,609
Look, you made him freeze up.

260
00:11:19,633 --> 00:11:21,733
I didn't mean to, I didn't mean to.

261
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:23,167
Hey.

262
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,633
What's wrong with that?

263
00:11:34,433 --> 00:11:37,133
I love BL too.

264
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:40,567
What's so weird about it?

265
00:11:42,333 --> 00:11:45,033
Serizawa...

266
00:11:47,033 --> 00:11:48,600
You guys are so pathetic.

267
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,633
Just because you don't understand it,

268
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:55,367
don't trash what other people care about!

269
00:11:55,467 --> 00:11:59,200
No... I didn't mean it like that...

270
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:01,000
What's going on?

271
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:02,567
Are you guys fighting?

272
00:12:02,667 --> 00:12:04,833
I thought I heard you talking about BL.

273
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:06,100
Uh, well...

274
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:08,433
More importantly, who are you guys?

275
00:12:09,167 --> 00:12:16,167
Uh... they were my
friends in freshman year.

276
00:12:18,867 --> 00:12:20,667
People who used to be my friends...

277
00:12:26,467 --> 00:12:31,000
I don't know if you're
ex-friends or what,

278
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:36,000
but could you stop bothering our Suzuki?

279
00:12:37,367 --> 00:12:38,800
Sure thing.

280
00:12:39,267 --> 00:12:40,433
- Let's go.
- Okay...

281
00:12:40,767 --> 00:12:42,700
Matsuno... hurry up.

282
00:12:49,433 --> 00:12:50,667
Are you okay?

283
00:12:50,767 --> 00:12:51,833
Yeah.

284
00:12:51,933 --> 00:12:53,233
Thanks.

285
00:12:57,100 --> 00:12:58,667
What happened?

286
00:13:11,433 --> 00:13:14,000
Back in middle school,

287
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:17,167
I was really stressed out
about exams for a while.

288
00:13:18,267 --> 00:13:21,867
I wanted a change of pace,

289
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:24,867
and a BL drama popped
up in my recommendations.

290
00:13:24,967 --> 00:13:27,500
I just clicked on it on a whim.

291
00:13:30,733 --> 00:13:32,200
I'm here!

292
00:13:33,367 --> 00:13:34,533
Huh?

293
00:13:34,633 --> 00:13:35,633
Why?

294
00:13:41,433 --> 00:13:43,200
Didn't I say I'd come?

295
00:13:48,733 --> 00:13:51,167
Since it was a high school drama,

296
00:13:51,267 --> 00:13:54,800
at first, I just admired it,
wishing I could have

297
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:58,433
such a sparkling
high school life too.

298
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:00,667
Why?

299
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:05,467
I can't take it anymore.

300
00:14:05,567 --> 00:14:07,300
I'm so tired.

301
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,467
Me too.

302
00:14:29,467 --> 00:14:32,533
Before I knew it, I was completely hooked.

303
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:34,620
The more I watched, the deeper I fell.

304
00:14:35,767 --> 00:14:38,467
Then I started reading
novels and manga too.

305
00:14:40,567 --> 00:14:42,633
And every single one was amazing.

306
00:14:43,933 --> 00:14:46,233
They were all such gentle worlds.

307
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:50,633
Only during those moments...

308
00:14:50,733 --> 00:14:53,700
could I forget everything I hated.

309
00:14:55,667 --> 00:14:59,500
But during my freshman year,

310
00:15:00,533 --> 00:15:02,600
I accidentally brought it up with them,

311
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:04,300
and they totally judged me for it.

312
00:15:08,833 --> 00:15:10,533
I seriously didn't sleep at all.

313
00:15:10,633 --> 00:15:12,400
Go to sleep then.

314
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:15,133
I have an event tomorrow, so I
have to pull another all-nighter.

315
00:15:15,233 --> 00:15:17,343
- You're way too obsessed with mobile games.
- Give it a rest.

316
00:15:17,367 --> 00:15:18,200
What about you, Suzuki?

317
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:20,833
I've been really into BL lately.

318
00:15:20,933 --> 00:15:22,000
Huh?

319
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:23,167
BL?

320
00:15:23,267 --> 00:15:24,609
Like, guys falling in love with guys?

321
00:15:24,633 --> 00:15:26,867
Yeah, it's really good.
It's just a love story.

322
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:28,333
And it makes your heart flutter.

323
00:15:28,433 --> 00:15:30,209
It makes you feel like you
can truly fall for someone.

324
00:15:30,233 --> 00:15:31,933
It's really nice.

325
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:38,100
Wait, Suzuki, are you one of those?

326
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:40,500
Huh? One of what?

327
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,867
You know...

328
00:15:43,267 --> 00:15:44,267
Ah...

329
00:15:50,167 --> 00:15:53,967
Are you and Matsuno in
that kind of relationship?

330
00:15:54,067 --> 00:15:56,600
What are you talking about?

331
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:57,433
Of course not.

332
00:15:57,533 --> 00:16:00,000
- That's gross.
- Hey, knock it off.

333
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:02,333
- You guys make a cute couple.
- No, we don't.

334
00:16:02,433 --> 00:16:03,443
- Stop it.
- Give him a hug!

335
00:16:03,467 --> 00:16:05,476
- Are you a top or a bottom?
- Don't get the wrong idea.

336
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:06,709
- What top or bottom?
- Which one is it?

337
00:16:06,733 --> 00:16:07,300
Aren't you gay?

338
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:08,400
That's not true at all.

339
00:16:08,567 --> 00:16:09,067
Seriously.

340
00:16:09,167 --> 00:16:11,533
- You're lying, right?
- Yeah, totally.

341
00:16:16,533 --> 00:16:20,367
Since then, I kept it a
secret from everyone.

342
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:22,933
I just enjoyed it by myself.

343
00:16:29,533 --> 00:16:33,433
Ah... sorry for bringing
this up out of nowhere.

344
00:16:34,333 --> 00:16:35,900
It's fine.

345
00:16:36,367 --> 00:16:38,367
If you like BL,

346
00:16:38,467 --> 00:16:40,043
doesn't that make you just like Serizawa?

347
00:16:40,067 --> 00:16:43,167
Oh, is that how you guys got close?

348
00:16:43,267 --> 00:16:44,500
Yeah.

349
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:48,667
Actually, I write novels based on Serizawa.

350
00:16:48,767 --> 00:16:49,633
What!?

351
00:16:49,733 --> 00:16:51,200
Suzuki, you write novels too?

352
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:52,000
That's awesome.

353
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:54,200
I want to read your novels too, Suzuki.

354
00:16:55,067 --> 00:16:57,200
Plus, I like BL as well.

355
00:16:57,300 --> 00:16:58,309
You like it too, Takeuchi?

356
00:16:58,333 --> 00:17:01,500
To be honest, I've been
reading it longer than Serizawa.

357
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:03,133
We've read it too.

358
00:17:03,233 --> 00:17:05,733
Yeah, Serizawa kept forcing it on us.

359
00:17:05,833 --> 00:17:07,900
I've read manga.

360
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,533
It's actually pretty good.

361
00:17:09,626 --> 00:17:10,626
He only reads manga.

362
00:17:10,733 --> 00:17:12,333
Yeah.

363
00:17:17,100 --> 00:17:18,300
What's wrong?

364
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,900
Suzuki.

365
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:23,367
Nothing, I just feel like...

366
00:17:24,667 --> 00:17:26,867
this world is so gentle.

367
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:33,700
See, what did I tell you?

368
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:37,100
They don't care about stuff like that.

369
00:17:40,433 --> 00:17:45,267
But out of everyone in the world, I'm
the one who wants to treat Suzuki the best.

370
00:17:51,733 --> 00:17:53,733
What's gotten into you?

371
00:17:54,267 --> 00:17:56,300
I think I can sing now.

372
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:57,633
Wait... now!?

373
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,967
That's the spirit, Suzuki!

374
00:18:00,067 --> 00:18:01,067
Come on, sing it.

375
00:18:01,133 --> 00:18:01,467
Okay.

376
00:18:01,567 --> 00:18:03,067
Go for it, Suzuki!

377
00:18:03,167 --> 00:18:04,500
Nice, let's go.

378
00:18:09,333 --> 00:18:11,100
Get ready.

379
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:13,333
Show 'em what you got.

380
00:18:14,467 --> 00:18:15,000
Here we go.

381
00:18:15,467 --> 00:18:21,433
♪ Chasing rabbits on that mountain ♪

382
00:18:21,533 --> 00:18:24,367
♪ Hey! ♪

383
00:18:24,467 --> 00:18:31,167
♪ Catching minnows in that stream ♪

384
00:18:31,667 --> 00:18:33,033
♪ Hey! ♪

385
00:18:33,133 --> 00:18:35,500
- ♪ Still swirling in my dreams ♪
- Don't worry about it.

386
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:36,300
Keep it up, Suzuki!

387
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:40,267
♪ Unforgettable is my hometown ♪

388
00:18:45,533 --> 00:18:47,667
Oh crap, run!

389
00:18:47,767 --> 00:18:48,367
Here.

390
00:18:48,467 --> 00:18:49,467
Here.

391
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:51,600
Give it back.

392
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:52,167
Here you go.

393
00:18:52,267 --> 00:18:53,267
Okay.

394
00:18:53,433 --> 00:18:54,667
We're doomed.

395
00:18:54,767 --> 00:18:59,467
So, how did it feel? Singing in
front of people for the first time?

396
00:18:59,733 --> 00:19:02,133
Ah, well...

397
00:19:02,767 --> 00:19:04,800
It wasn't quite what I expected.

398
00:19:05,667 --> 00:19:08,200
It felt like no one was
really listening to me sing.

399
00:19:08,300 --> 00:19:09,367
- Hey!
- Hey!

400
00:19:09,467 --> 00:19:13,200
Yeah... that's pretty much how it goes.

401
00:19:13,833 --> 00:19:15,409
But thanks to that, I realized something.

402
00:19:15,433 --> 00:19:16,767
Huh?

403
00:19:16,967 --> 00:19:21,633
You don't really need to care
so much about what others think.

404
00:19:22,167 --> 00:19:25,867
The things you cherish,

405
00:19:25,967 --> 00:19:28,567
just enjoy your own world to the fullest.

406
00:19:30,433 --> 00:19:33,267
Yeah, you're right.

407
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:37,200
Thank you, Serizawa.

408
00:19:38,133 --> 00:19:39,967
Thanks for inviting me today.

409
00:19:42,833 --> 00:19:45,800
And thanks for standing up for me.

410
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:49,067
It was nothing.

411
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:52,833
Oh, Suzuki, do you still have some time?

412
00:19:53,167 --> 00:19:54,467
Huh?

413
00:20:01,067 --> 00:20:03,833
(Banana Lake)

414
00:20:03,933 --> 00:20:06,033
Looks so good...

415
00:20:09,667 --> 00:20:12,533
We come here all the time.

416
00:20:13,133 --> 00:20:16,200
The fries here are amazing.

417
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:19,367
Especially with the
truffle mayo, it's the best.

418
00:20:19,467 --> 00:20:22,167
I recommend the pesto pasta.

419
00:20:22,267 --> 00:20:24,533
No... you gotta try the
fried chicken and pudding.

420
00:20:25,433 --> 00:20:26,667
Pudding...

421
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:28,067
Which one are you craving?

422
00:20:28,167 --> 00:20:29,967
Suzuki, what do you want to eat first?

423
00:20:30,067 --> 00:20:31,100
Come on.

424
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:33,633
- This one is the best.
- No, this one is better.

425
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:34,467
Pesto...

426
00:20:34,567 --> 00:20:35,367
Fries!

427
00:20:35,467 --> 00:20:36,900
- Pudding...
- Pesto pasta.

428
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,067
Hmm?

429
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,800
Are you actually not hungry?

430
00:20:44,633 --> 00:20:46,100
I see...

431
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:47,767
Well, nothing we can do about that.

432
00:20:49,433 --> 00:20:50,433
No...

433
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:52,433
It's not that.

434
00:20:52,933 --> 00:20:54,100
Yeah.

435
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:57,667
I'm just feeling the fun.

436
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:01,733
And I...

437
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:06,733
I'm just so happy right now.

438
00:21:13,133 --> 00:21:14,733
So cute.

439
00:21:16,367 --> 00:21:17,367
Cute?

440
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:18,200
Me?

441
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:20,233
Who else would I be talking about?

442
00:21:20,333 --> 00:21:22,667
You're seriously way too cute.

443
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:25,700
Here, just eat something first.

444
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:27,533
Say ah.

445
00:21:28,633 --> 00:21:29,533
Oh?

446
00:21:29,633 --> 00:21:30,267
He ate it!

447
00:21:30,367 --> 00:21:31,467
Hey, that's not fair!

448
00:21:31,567 --> 00:21:32,576
Suzuki, eat this too. Have mine.

449
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:33,500
Say ah.

450
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:36,200
I've got some too, with mayo on it.

451
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:36,900
Come on.

452
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,833
Hey, you guys, stop feeding
my Suzuki without permission.

453
00:21:39,933 --> 00:21:40,467
Ah.

454
00:21:40,567 --> 00:21:42,233
You've got some nerve saying "feeding."

455
00:21:42,333 --> 00:21:43,609
And he's not "your" Suzuki, okay?

456
00:21:43,633 --> 00:21:44,733
Exactly.

457
00:21:44,833 --> 00:21:45,733
Suzuki belongs to everyone.

458
00:21:45,833 --> 00:21:46,533
Yeah.

459
00:21:46,633 --> 00:21:48,143
- What the heck?
- Suzuki belongs to us.

460
00:21:48,167 --> 00:21:49,000
What, you wanna fight?

461
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:50,443
Bring it on! I'll take you all on.

462
00:21:50,467 --> 00:21:51,633
Here I come.

463
00:21:51,733 --> 00:21:54,300
Alright, I'm fully charged.

464
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,533
Okay...

465
00:21:55,633 --> 00:21:56,976
- It's too late to back out now.
- Wait...

466
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:58,367
Wait, stop fighting!

467
00:21:59,067 --> 00:22:00,667
We're just kidding.

468
00:22:00,767 --> 00:22:02,143
- Sorry about that.
- Thank goodness.

469
00:22:02,167 --> 00:22:03,167
- Pow!
- Ouch!

470
00:22:03,233 --> 00:22:04,393
What are you saying ouch for?

471
00:22:05,567 --> 00:22:09,633
Anyway, I'm number one in Suzuki's heart.

472
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,467
Right?

473
00:22:19,133 --> 00:22:20,033
Let's eat before it gets cold.

474
00:22:20,133 --> 00:22:21,267
Come on.

475
00:22:22,767 --> 00:22:23,767
Let's eat.

476
00:22:34,233 --> 00:22:35,267
It's really good.

477
00:22:44,367 --> 00:22:47,267
(Next Episode Preview)
Suzuki, do you like Serizawa?

478
00:22:47,367 --> 00:22:47,867
Huh?

479
00:22:47,967 --> 00:22:49,167
I told you it's not like that.

480
00:22:49,533 --> 00:22:50,600
I really want to see you.

481
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:52,300
I can feed myself.

482
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:54,367
- I should probably head back...
- Don't go.

483
00:22:54,467 --> 00:22:55,767
Stay with me until morning.

484
00:22:56,333 --> 00:22:59,000
(This drama is purely fictional)
Is this how friends act?
